    "description": "U.S. Medical Outpatient Facilities Portfolio (Montecito JV) is a portfolio of medical outpatient properties in the United States. Its end users are patients and physician practices requiring ambulatory surgery, radiology, oncology, orthopedics, and related outpatient services. The model is asset-heavy and healthcare-oriented, with economics supported by specialized outpatient real estate rather than general office tenancy. Fengate disclosed in 2025 that the acquisition covered 16 facilities serving communities across 10 states and formed part of a healthcare portfolio exceeding 80 facilities and more than US$1 billion in assets. The reviewed materials did not disclose property-level revenue or current ownership percentages within the joint venture. Fengate completed the acquisition alongside Montecito Medical in 2025 on behalf of Fengate Infrastructure Fund IV and affiliated entities.",
